{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Close gate REFUSED — `file_impact` omits a file AC1 forces the work to touch\n\nThe close was attempted from `.rebar/worktrees/impl-db2c` at `ad119195efa`, with the merge\n`374cc2f22b1` reachable. The completion precheck refused:\n\n```\ncannot close: commit 374cc2f22b1 changes src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py,\nwhich the recorded file_impact does not declare, so the work went beyond the\nreviewed plan.\n```\n\n**The gate is right, and this is a plan defect rather than scope creep.** The touch is not\noptional — AC1 is `git grep -lF 'rebar._engine_support.resolver' -- src scripts` exiting 1\nwith no output, and `resolver.py`'s own module docstring contained that exact literal:\n\n```\n-helpers — by re-exporting them, so every existing\n-``from rebar._engine_support.resolver import …`` importer is unchanged.\n+helpers — by re-exporting them, so every existing importer of this module is\n+unchanged.\n```\n\nSo the plan's AC1 **requires** editing `resolver.py`, while the plan's `file_impact`\n**omits** it. The change is docstring-only; the re-export surface is untouched, so AC6's\n\"shim deliberately retained\" property still holds and nothing about the implementation\nwent beyond the reviewed intent.\n\n### Status\n\nAll 10 ACs pass on the landed tree (previous comment). The change is **merged** as\n`374cc2f22b1` with `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`. Only the ticket close is blocked.\n\nThe non-force path is `set-file-impact` to add `src/rebar/_engine_support/resolver.py`,\nwhich is a material plan change and so invalidates the attestation (`stale-material`),\nrequiring `review-plan` to be re-run before the close succeeds. That costs a full\nplan-review pass on a ticket whose code has already landed and been verified. Escalated to\nthe operator rather than forced — agents do not use `--force` on this project.\n\n**New instance of the planning defect class:** `file_impact` that omits a file the\nticket's own acceptance criteria compel the implementation to modify. Distinct from the\nlatent-AC count defect, and detectable at plan time by checking every AC's grep scope\nagainst the declared `file_impact`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793406570309952688,"uuid":"faa48ef2-84af-459d-ac1c-93fa8c4e4f99"}